**Schedule amendment charge.** With build time equal to source time minus 5.5 s, CP2 has bar 4 already drawing at **1500 ms**, while the Plan starts it at **1900 ms** (`1000 + 3 × 300`). CP3 has four complete empty outlines at **2500 ms**, while the Plan completes them at **2800 ms** (`1900 + 900`). CP8 has a solid fourth bar and its 100% label at **8500 ms**, while the fill completes at **8600 ms** (`7700 + 900`). The printed tolerances leave those sampled-state contradictions intact. Revise the defaults to satisfy all three states and reconcile the table with §2b’s two-stage exit. The amended exit reaches absence at **10500 ms** (`10000 + 500`), and the timing swap yields full completion at **9200 ms** (`8600 + 600`), ahead of the **9500 ms** fill-clear start. Those parts of the addendum hold. [Item census and schedule](item-T242-observe-plan.md#L19) · [Plan addendum](item-T242-observe-plan.md#L73)

The remapped table also needs the second group-label reveal at CP7 and the elements that persist through fill clearance. The Latin label substitution is declared. The perimeter-motion simplification and any omission of the group-label reveal need an explicit disposition. The filed Observe gate gave `mechanics-seen` and `variables-extracted` full credit, and the relevant states are already on record. This is a Plan revision. [Item census, CP7](item-T242-observe-plan.md#L28) · [Observe audit, finding 2](item-T242-codex-observe-return.md#L5) · [Observe-exit findings](item-T242-jev-observe-exit-return.md#L7)

